In a session of a D&D (5e) game for a six-year-old boy playing a level 2 chaotic evil Tiefling named Ekemon, the DM plans a temple raid as a mini-dungeon crawl. The session revolves around Ekemon and two pirate allies raiding the Temple of the Ember Dragon, which holds treasures and a magical relic called a "Heart-Ember." Upon defeating the boss cleric, they find 35 gp, 70 sp, two golden dragon idols (25 gp each), and a silver sun-disc (15 gp). Additionally, they discover treasure items like an **Ember Cloak** and a **Potion of Fire Breath**. The open book on the altar provides lore about the Ember Titan and hints at the dragonborn's whereabouts, tying the adventure to future quests in the **Redclaw Peaks**. The DM suggests awarding about 350 XP to Ekemon for the entire dungeon, allowing him to possibly level up.
